</span></td>
<td id="S3.T2.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="S3.T2.2.3.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:113.8pt;">
<span id="S3.T2.2.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.T2.2.3.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">I6 (Layer-class compatibility)</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S3.T2.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="S3.T2.2.3.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:184.9pt;">
<span id="S3.T2.2.3.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.T2.2.3.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Hard constraints are hosted at the orchestration, tool, or policy layer, never solely at the prompt layer; constraints are not subject to model reinterpretation.</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.T2.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S3.T2.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb">
<span id="S3.T2.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:99.6pt;">
<span id="S3.T2.2.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.T2.2.4.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Verifiability</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S3.T2.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb">
<span id="S3.T2.2.4.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:113.8pt;">
<span id="S3.T2.2.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.T2.2.4.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">I8 (Specification-trace correspondence)</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S3.T2.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb">
<span id="S3.T2.2.4.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:184.9pt;">
<span id="S3.T2.2.4.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.T2.2.4.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The trace is machine-checkable against the specification; every action’s constraint evaluation is reconstructible from the SARC tuple.</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span>Mapping between classical reference monitor properties and SARC invariants. The framework instantiates the three reference monitor requirements within the agent execution loop, with PAG, ATM, PAA, and ER serving as the concrete enforcement points.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsection" style="font-size:120%;--ltx-fg-color:#1F3A5F;">3.6  Specification-Trace Correspondence as a Checkable Property</h3>

<div id="S3.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The auditability invariant I8 can be stated as a formal property of SARC-governed executions. We give the definition here so that “auditable by construction” has a precise computational meaning rather than a rhetorical one.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 2</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Specification-trace correspondence)<span id="Thmdefinition2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma=\langle S,A,R,C\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma=\langle S,A,R,C\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> be a SARC specification and let <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=\langle t_{1},t_{2},\ldots,t_{n}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=\langle t_{1},t_{2},\ldots,t_{n}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> be a runtime trace, where each <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is a record of the form</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}=\langle s_{i},a_{i},s^{\prime}_{i},r_{i},\text{obs}_{i},E_{i},\alpha_{i}\rangle," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">obs</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}=\langle s_{i},a_{i},s^{\prime}_{i},r_{i},\text{obs}_{i},E_{i},\alpha_{i}\rangle,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmdefinition2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">with <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{i}\subseteq C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{i}\subseteq C</annotation></semantics></math> the set of constraints whose evaluation outcomes are recorded for action <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> the attribution tuple. We say that <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> is in correspondence with <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>, written <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\models\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⊧</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\models\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>, iff for every <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}\in T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}\in T</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<ol id="S3.I3" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:2em;">
<li id="S3.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S3.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S3.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph">(Coverage)</em><span id="S3.I3.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> For every </span><math id="S3.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\in C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\in C</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I3.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> such that </span><math id="S3.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I3.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> applies to </span><math id="S3.I3.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I3.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> in state </span><math id="S3.I3.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I3.i1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="S3.I3.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\in E_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\in E_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I3.i1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> or </span><math id="S3.I3.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I3.i1.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> has been evaluated at the decidability-rescue layer </span><math id="S3.I3.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I3.i1.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> of §</span><a href="#S9.SS2" title="9.2 Constraint Propagation under Recursion ‣ 9 Multi-Agent Systems Under SARC ‣ SARC: A Governance-by-Architecture Frameworkfor Agentic AI SystemsCompiling Regulatory Obligations into Runtime Constraints" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9.2</span></a><span id="S3.I3.i1.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and the rescue is recorded.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S3.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S3.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph">(Class-placement compatibility)</em><span id="S3.I3.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> For every </span><math id="S3.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\in E_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\in E_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I3.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, the verification point at which </span><math id="S3.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I3.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> was evaluated is compatible with </span><math id="S3.I3.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{class}(c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">class</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{class}(c)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I3.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> as declared in </span><math id="S3.I3.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I3.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> (hard constraints not solely at the prompt layer; escalation constraints with bounded reversibility window; etc.).</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S3.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S3.I3.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph">(Outcome consistency)</em><span id="S3.I3.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> For every </span><math id="S3.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\in E_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\in E_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I3.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> that fired, the recorded response in </span><math id="S3.I3.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I3.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is the response declared by </span><math id="S3.I3.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c.\texttt{resp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">resp</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c.\texttt{resp}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I3.i3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> in </span><math id="S3.I3.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I3.i3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I3.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="S3.I3.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I3.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S3.I3.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph">(Attribution completeness)</em><span id="S3.I3.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> The attribution tuple </span><math id="S3.I3.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I3.i4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> resolves to a non-empty principal-and-agent chain whose intersected authority is non-empty.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmproperty1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_property">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproperty1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Property 1</span></span><span id="Thmproperty1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Decidable audit)<span id="Thmproperty1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproperty1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproperty1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproperty1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any finite <math id="Thmproperty1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> and finite trace <math id="Thmproperty1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>, the question “does <math id="Thmproperty1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\models\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⊧</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\models\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> hold?” is decidable in time <math id="Thmproperty1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(|T|\cdot|C|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>T</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(|T|\cdot|C|)</annotation></semantics></math> given that each constraint’s predicate is itself decidable in bounded time at its declared verification point. The check requires no access to the model that produced the trace or to its prompts.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The decidable-audit property is the formal content of “auditable by construction.” It states that an external auditor, given <math id="S3.SS6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>, can mechanically verify whether the system honored its specification, without requiring access to the model, the developers, or the deployment’s institutional context. The check operates as a function over two artifacts that the framework requires the system to produce: the specification (declared at design time, versioned per §<a href="#S6.SS4.SSS0.Px3" title="The translation layer. ‣ 6.4 Annex III Mapping ‣ 6 Compiling Regulatory Obligations into Runtime Checks ‣ SARC: A Governance-by-Architecture Frameworkfor Agentic AI SystemsCompiling Regulatory Obligations into Runtime Constraints" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.4</span></a>) and the trace (emitted at runtime per Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 7 The SARC-Governed Agent Loop ‣ SARC: A Governance-by-Architecture Frameworkfor Agentic AI SystemsCompiling Regulatory Obligations into Runtime Constraints" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS6.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">What an audit checker does.</h4>

<div id="S3.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A checker implementing Definition <a href="#Thmdefinition2" title="Definition 2 (Specification-trace correspondence). ‣ 3.6 Specification-Trace Correspondence as a Checkable Property ‣ 3 The SARC Construct ‣ SARC: A Governance-by-Architecture Frameworkfor Agentic AI SystemsCompiling Regulatory Obligations into Runtime Constraints" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> performs four passes over <math id="S3.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>: (i) for each <math id="S3.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, enumerate constraints in <math id="S3.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> applicable to <math id="S3.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and check coverage against <math id="S3.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>; (ii) for each evaluated constraint, check that the verification point recorded in <math id="S3.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is compatible with the constraint’s declared class; (iii) for each fired constraint, check that the response recorded in <math id="S3.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> matches <math id="S3.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c.\texttt{resp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">resp</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c.\texttt{resp}</annotation></semantics></math>; (iv) for each <math id="S3.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, check that <math id="S3.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is well-formed and that the implied authority chain is non-empty. Failures at any pass produce a structured discrepancy report identifying the action, the constraint, and the violated condition. We have implemented this checker as a Python function, included as supplementary material at <a href="https://github.com/besanson/sarc-governance" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/besanson/sarc-governance</a>, operating over JSON specifications and runtime traces. The implementation is deterministic, predicate-language-agnostic, and bounded by tool latency rather than by model latency, in keeping with the framework’s design rule that audit decisions should not depend on model inference. We exercise the checker on every SARC trace produced in the evaluation of §<a href="#S10" title="10 Empirical Evaluation: SARC vs. Practitioner Baselines ‣ SARC: A Governance-by-Architecture Frameworkfor Agentic AI SystemsCompiling Regulatory Obligations into Runtime Constraints" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_section" style="font-size:144%;--ltx-fg-color:#1F3A5F;">4  Reference Runtime Architecture</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The contribution of SARC is not the four-tuple as a paper artifact; it is the four-tuple as an architectural commitment. This section makes the commitment concrete by specifying a reference runtime in which <math id="S4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is enforced at four named points.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsection" style="font-size:120%;--ltx-fg-color:#1F3A5F;">4.1  The Four Enforcement Points</h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S4.I1" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:2em;">
<li id="S4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pre-Action Gate (PAG).</span> Evaluated before an action is dispatched. Predicate of the form <math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(s,a)</annotation></semantics></math>. Used for hard constraints and predictive escalations decidable from state and contemplated action alone.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Action-Time Monitor (ATM).</span> Evaluated during action execution, typically through wrapping of the tool call. Used for constraints that depend on partial outputs (cost accumulation, latency budget, content classification on streaming returns). Can interrupt mid-flight.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Post-Action Auditor (PAA).</span> Evaluated after an action completes, before the next agent step. Used for constraints that compare post-action state to pre-action state (drift, side-effect verification). Cannot prevent the just-completed action; can prevent the next.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Escalation Router (ER).</span> Stateless component invoked by the above. Routes a flagged action to the appropriate human operator, persists the decision, and returns control to the agent loop. §<a href="#S5.SS3" title="5.3 Escalation Queueing ‣ 5 Operational Trade-offs: Latency, Calibration, Queueing ‣ SARC: A Governance-by-Architecture Frameworkfor Agentic AI SystemsCompiling Regulatory Obligations into Runtime Constraints" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a> characterizes its queueing behavior.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F1" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S4.F1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="256.7" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 633.55 256.7" width="633.55"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="translate(0,256.7) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(226.66,0) translate(0,128.35)"><g stroke-width="0.4pt"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#1F3A5F;--ltx-fill-color:#E8EEF4;" fill="#E8EEF4" stroke="#1F3A5F"><path d="M 223.61 16.73 L -223.61 16.73 C -225.14 16.73 -226.38 15.49 -226.38 13.96 L -226.38 -13.96 C -226.38 -15.49 -225.14 -16.73 -223.61 -16.73 L 223.61 -16.73 C 225.14 -16.73 226.38 -15.49 226.38 -13.96 L 226.38 13.96 C 226.38 15.49 225.14 16.73 223.61 16.73 Z M -226.38 -16.73"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -176.69 -3.11)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:26em;--ltx-fo-height:0.73em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.24em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="12.45" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.34)" width="332.76"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S4.F1.pic1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Orchestration Layer </span><span id="S4.F1.pic1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(planner <math id="S4.F1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cdot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⋅</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cdot</annotation></semantics></math> memory <math id="S4.F1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cdot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⋅</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cdot</annotation></semantics></math> tool dispatcher)</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#1F3A5F;--ltx-fill-color:#E8EEF4;" fill="#E8EEF4" stroke="#1F3A5F"><path d="M 223.61 -38.94 L -223.61 -38.94 C -225.14 -38.94 -226.38 -40.18 -226.38 -41.71 L -226.38 -69.64 C -226.38 -71.16 -225.14 -72.4 -223.61 -72.4 L 223.61 -72.4 C 225.14 -72.4 226.38 -71.16 226.38 -69.64 L 226.38 -41.71 C 226.38 -40.18 225.14 -38.94 223.61 -38.94 Z M -226.38 -72.4"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -153.84 -58.78)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:22.71em;--ltx-fo-height:0.73em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.24em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="12.45" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.34)" width="290.68"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S4.F1.pic1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Tool Layer </span><span id="S4.F1.pic1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(typed tool registry <math id="S4.F1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cdot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⋅</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cdot</annotation></semantics></math> external systems)</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#1F3A5F;--ltx-fill-color:#E8EEF4;" fill="#E8EEF4" stroke="#1F3A5F"><path d="M 223.61 -94.61 L -223.61 -94.61 C -225.14 -94.61 -226.38 -95.85 -226.38 -97.38 L -226.38 -125.31 C -226.38 -126.84 -225.14 -128.08 -223.61 -128.08 L 223.61 -128.08 C 225.14 -128.08 226.38 -126.84 226.38 -125.31 L 226.38 -97.38 C 226.38 -95.85 225.14 -94.61 223.61 -94.61 Z M -226.38 -128.08"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -206.44 -114.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:30.49em;--ltx-fo-height:0.73em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.24em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="12.45" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.34)" width="390.24"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S4.F1.pic1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Environment / World </span><span id="S4.F1.pic1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(databases <math id="S4.F1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cdot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⋅</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cdot</annotation></semantics></math> APIs <math id="S4.F1.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cdot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⋅</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cdot</annotation></semantics></math> humans <math id="S4.F1.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cdot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⋅</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cdot</annotation></semantics></math> physical assets)</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#1F3A5F;--ltx-fill-color:#E8EEF4;" fill="#E8EEF4" stroke="#1F3A5F"><path d="M 223.61 72.4 L -223.61 72.4 C -225.14 72.4 -226.38 71.16 -226.38 69.64 L -226.38 41.71 C -226.38 40.18 -225.14 38.94 -223.61 38.94 L 223.61 38.94 C 225.14 38.94 226.38 40.18 226.38 41.71 L 226.38 69.64 C 226.38 71.16 225.14 72.4 223.61 72.4 Z M -226.38 38.94"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -157.34 52.56)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:22.91em;--ltx-fo-height:0.73em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.24em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="12.45" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.34)" width="293.25"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S4.F1.pic1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Model Layer </span><span id="S4.F1.pic1.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(LLM <math id="S4.F1.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cdot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⋅</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cdot</annotation></semantics></math> reasoning <math id="S4.F1.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cdot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⋅</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cdot</annotation></semantics></math> planning prompts)</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#1F3A5F;--ltx-fill-color:#DDE1E7;" fill="#DDE1E7" stroke="#1F3A5F"><path d="M 223.61 128.08 L -223.61 128.08 C -225.14 128.08 -226.38 126.84 -226.38 125.31 L -226.38 97.38 C -226.38 95.85 -225.14 94.61 -223.61 94.61 L 223.61 94.61 C 225.14 94.61 226.38 95.85 226.38 97.38 L 226.38 125.31 C 226.38 126.84 225.14 128.08 223.61 128.08 Z M -226.38 94.61"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -87.29 107.88)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:5.86em;--ltx-fo-height:0.59em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10.65pt;" height="11.07" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="86.38"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S4.F1.pic1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Specification </span><math id="S4.F1.pic1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma=\langle S,A,R,C\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">S</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">A</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">R</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">C</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma=\langle S,A,R,C\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#B71C1C;--ltx-fill-color:#F8E8E8;" fill="#F8E8E8" stroke="#B71C1C"><path d="M 374.11 22.64 L 245.45 22.64 C 243.92 22.64 242.68 21.4 242.68 19.87 L 242.68 3.